    {
      "id": "M4115-A",
      "prompt": "A. A fictional multirate process model encodes each sampling stream at its native length. A learned linear layer maps each encoded sequence to length T, and a contrastive training objective relates paired views of the same underlying stream. The trained representations feed a fault classifier. No raw-data interpolation or missing-value output is implemented. The draft abstract says: 'A temporal synchronization module restores missing measurements and aligns all physical sampling instants. The synchronized data are fused for diagnosis.' Give two connected English replacement sentences and a brief Chinese rationale. The author wants to preserve the model, not add another module.",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Describe encoded-length mapping and contrastive training as distinct operations supplying classification.",
        "Preserve the lack of measurement completion or physical timestamp correspondence."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Invent raw interpolation, completed measurements or synchronized acquisition.",
        "Turn a training objective into a sequential inference-time fusion operation."
      ],
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "outcome": "pass",
