      "evaluation_phase": "fresh_context_frozen_candidate",
      "baseline_outcome": "not_run"
    },
    {
      "id": "M4115-B",
      "prompt": "B. A fictional domain-adaptation classifier is trained with labeled source samples, unlabeled target samples, source cross-entropy and MMD between the pooled source and target feature distributions. It has no target pseudolabels or class-conditional term. At inference it uses only the encoder and classifier. Its contribution says: 'The alignment module matches every source sample to a target sample of the same fault class and guarantees fault-discriminative cross-condition features.' Rewrite that item in English and give the minimum Chinese checks needed before claiming diagnostic benefit. No performance results or novelty comparison have been supplied.",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Keep marginal distribution matching and source classification in the training phase.",
        "Separate intended purpose, observed benefit and novelty; require claim-matched target evaluation."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Invent sample correspondences, target labels or class-conditional alignment.",
        "Guarantee class semantics or present standard MMD use as proven novelty."
      ],
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "outcome": "pass",
      "language": "en+zh",
      "tested_skills": [
