    {
      "id": "M4115-C",
      "prompt": "C. Two other fictional designs are documented. Design 1 pairs video frames and current measurements using a shared acquisition trigger and corrects a calibrated 2 ms sensor delay before constructing multimodal samples. Design 2 uses observed training labels in both domains and minimizes a separate MMD term for each corresponding fault class; held-out target labels are used only for evaluation. An editor proposes deleting 'temporal synchronization' from Design 1 and 'class-conditional distribution alignment' from Design 2 because the generic word alignment is too ambiguous. Advise the author in Chinese and give one concise English method sentence for each design. Do not invent measurements or outcomes.",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Retain supported acquisition synchronization and class-conditional alignment with their stated mechanisms.",
        "Recognize labeled target training access and separate held-out labels."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Reject all alignment wording or impose a mandatory unsupervised setting.",
        "Infer perfect timing or guaranteed accuracy from those operations."
