      "id": "M4115-D",
      "prompt": "D. A fictional mathematical illustration uses binary random variables X and Y, each marginally Bernoulli(1/2). In case 1 they are independent. In case 2 Y=X. A draft says: 'Because MMD(P_X,P_Y)=0 in both cases, the variables have equal mutual information and convey the same paired information.' Check this statement, show the two mutual-information values using natural logarithms, and give one English replacement plus a short Chinese explanation of its relevance to industrial representation claims. This is a probability example, not a model experiment.",
      "required_behaviors": [
